@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Direct messages for buyers - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Buying items";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Direct messages for buyers";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0.4), rgba(0,0,0,0.4)), url('/help_centre_img/help_area/help_centre_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Direct messages (DMs) let you communicate with sellers and other Lively users directly on the platform.</p>

        <p><strong>As a buyer, use DMs to:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Ask questions about a seller's products</li>
            <li>Coordinate shipping details</li>
            <li>Resolve order issues directly with sellers</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Keeping conversations on Lively helps protect both you and sellers, and allows us to support the transaction if something goes wrong.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#send-a-message">Send a message</a></li>
            <li><a href="#manage-messages">Manage messages in your Inbox</a></li>
            <li><a href="#block-or-report">Block or report someone from messages</a></li>
            <li><a href="#turn-dms-on-or-off">Turn direct messages on or off</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="use-dms-safely">Use direct messages safely</h2>

        <p>All messages on Lively must follow our <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">Community Guidelines</a>.</p>

        <p>To help protect our community:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Keep buying, selling, and payments on Lively.</strong> Don't ask for or accept payment, purchases, or sales outside the platform.</li>
            <li><strong>Don't share personal contact information to move transactions off-platform.</strong> This includes phone numbers, email addresses, or social media handles.</li>
            <li><strong>Report users who ask to move transactions off-platform.</strong> If another user asks you to buy, sell, or pay outside of Lively, <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">report the conversation</a> so we can investigate and help keep the community safe.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Lively can't provide support for transactions that happen outside the platform. Participating in or encouraging off-platform activity may result in <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">account action</a>, including suspension or ban.</p>

        <p>To help protect users and prevent fraud, Lively may review messages sent on the platform.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="access-inbox">Access messages in your Inbox</h2>

        <p>You can access all of your messages from your Inbox on the Lively app or web.</p>

        <p><strong>To open your Inbox:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Tap the <strong>messages icon</strong> on the Home screen.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="text-center my-4">
            <img src="/help_centre_img/help_area/access_messages.png"
                 alt="Rate purchase screen in Lively app"
                 class="img-fluid"
                 style="border-radius: 12px;" />
        </div>

        <p>If you have selling access, you'll see additional tabs in your Inbox. Learn about <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">direct messages for sellers</a>.</p>

        <div class="article-note-box">
            <strong>Note:</strong> If you've communicated with our Support team, those messages will appear in your email, not in your Lively Inbox.
        </div>
        <hr />

        <h2 id="send-a-message">Send a message</h2>

        <p>You can send a message from several places on Lively, including your Inbox, orders you've purchased, and people's profiles. No matter where you start, all conversations will appear in your Inbox.</p>

        <p><strong>Keep in mind:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>You can only message someone if they're <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">opted in to DMs</a> and they haven't <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">blocked</a> you.</li>
            <li>You can create group messages with up to 20 users.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="article-accordion-yellow">

            <div class="article-accordion-yellow__item">
                <button class="article-accordion-yellow__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__icon">−</span>
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__title">
                        From your Inbox
                    </span>
                </button>

                <div class="article-accordion-yellow__content">
                    <ol>
                        <li>From Lively's Home screen, open your <strong>Inbox</strong> (message icon).</li>
                        <li>Tap <strong>Compose.</strong></li>
                        <li>Enter the username.</li>
                        <li>Tap <strong>Start message.</strong></li>
                        <li>Type and send.</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="article-accordion-yellow__item is-collapsed">
                <button class="article-accordion-yellow__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__icon">−</span>
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__title">
                        From an order you've purchased
                    </span>
                </button>

                <div class="article-accordion-yellow__content">
                    <ol>
                        <li>Open your <strong>Activity</strong> tab.</li>
                        <li>Select the order.</li>
                        <li>Choose <strong>Message the seller.</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="manage-messages">Manage messages in your Inbox</h2>

        <div class="article-accordion-grey">

            <div class="article-accordion-grey__item">
                <button class="article-accordion-grey__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-grey__icon">−</span>
                    <span>Mark as Unread</span>
                </button>
                <div class="article-accordion-grey__content">
                    <p>Mark a message as unread if you want to come back to it later.</p>
                    <p><strong>To mark a message as unread:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>While viewing the message, tap the <strong>menu icon (three dots)</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Select <strong>Mark unread.</strong></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="article-accordion-grey__item is-collapsed">
                <button class="article-accordion-grey__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-grey__icon">−</span>
                    <span>Archive messages</span>
                </button>
                <div class="article-accordion-grey__content">
                    <p>Archive conversations you no longer need to keep your Inbox tidy. You can access archived messages again at any time.</p>
                    <p><strong>To archive a message:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>While viewing the message, tap the <strong>menu icon (three dots)</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Select <strong>Archive.</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                    <p><strong>To view archived messages:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>From the Home screen, tap your <strong>Inbox</strong> (message icon).</li>
                        <li>Tap the <strong>menu icon (≡)</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Select <strong>Archive.</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="article-accordion-grey__item is-collapsed">
                <button class="article-accordion-grey__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-grey__icon">−</span>
                    <span>View message requests</span>
                </button>
                <div class="article-accordion-grey__content">
                    <p>If you don't already have a connection with someone (for example, you don't mutually follow each other), their message may appear as a request instead of showing in your Inbox automatically.</p>
                    <p><strong>To view your message requests:</strong></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>From the Home screen, tap your <strong>Inbox</strong> (message icon).</li>
                        <li>Tap the <strong>menu icon (≡)</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Select <strong>Message requests.</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="block-or-report">Block or report someone from messages</h2>

        <p>Blocking someone prevents them from interacting with you again. If you report a message, our Trust &amp; Safety team will review it.</p>

        <ol>
            <li>Open the message.</li>
            <li>Tap the <strong>menu icon (three dots)</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Block</strong> or <strong>Report.</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="turn-dms-on-or-off">Turn direct messages on or off</h2>

        <p>You're automatically opted in to DMs, but you can turn them off at any time.</p>

        <p><strong>Keep in mind:</strong> Turning off DMs limits your ability to communicate with sellers 1:1 and may affect your buying experience.</p>

        <p><strong>To turn DMs on or off:</strong></p>
        <ol>
            <li>Tap or click your <strong>Account</strong> icon.</li>
            <li>(On web) Go to <strong>Account Settings.</strong></li>
            <li>Select <strong>Preferences.</strong></li>
            <li>Toggle <strong>Direct Messages</strong> on or off.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>